        "original_id": "d5340ed4-950c-5b0c-b9e8-5dd6d6091ec9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Short, Francis Poulenc\n- Organizations: Metropolitan Opera\n- Works: Dialogues des Carmélites, La Bohème, Don Carlos, La fanciulla del West, Ariadne auf Naxos, Turandot, Don Giovanni, Tosca, I Lombardi alla prima crociata, Madama Butterfly, Eugene Onegin\n- Roles: Colline, Friar, Happy, Jailer, Lackey, Mandarin, Masetto, Sciarrone, Pirro, Yamadori, Zaretsky\n\nFacts:\n- Francis Poulenc completed Dialogues des Carmélites in 1956.\n- Dialogues des Carmélites is a French opera in three acts, divided into twelve scenes with linking orchestral interludes, with music and libretto by Francis Poulenc.\n- Kevin Short performed at the Metropolitan Opera as Colline in La Bohème, the Friar in Don Carlos, Happy in La fanciulla del West, the Jailer in Dialogues des Carmélites, Lackey in Ariadne auf Naxos, Mandarin in Turandot, Masetto in Don Giovanni, Sciarrone in Tosca, Pirro in I Lombardi alla prima crociata, Yamadori in Madama Butterfly, and Zaretsky in Eugene Onegin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
